WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.300 --> 00:00:01.497
Warning! Warning!

2
00:00:01.497 --> 00:00:06.705
I built this with AI and text to speech, because I can't narrate for shit!

3
00:00:08.100 --> 00:00:09.223
Hey, Dreamer here.

4
00:00:09.223 --> 00:00:12.780
Today, abilities: the moves your characters can pull off,

5
00:00:12.780 --> 00:00:15.588
and the two numbers Voyage actually enforces.

6
00:00:17.000 --> 00:00:19.234
Open Mechanics, then Abilities.

7
00:00:19.234 --> 00:00:25.071
We've got three moves for our acts: Fan Throw, Slip the Cuffs, and Crowd Pleaser.

8
00:00:25.071 --> 00:00:28.819
Let's open Fan Throw and see what a move is made of.

9
00:00:29.267 --> 00:00:33.021
The description is everything the AI knows about the move.

10
00:00:33.021 --> 00:00:38.200
Mine starts with what it does in plain words, then how it looks when it happens.

11
00:00:38.200 --> 00:00:42.278
Area attacks, stuns, escapes: none of that has its own setting,

12
00:00:42.278 --> 00:00:44.673
so the description is where it lives.

13
00:00:45.133 --> 00:00:47.448
Requirements say who can learn it.

14
00:00:47.448 --> 00:00:50.036
Fan Throw needs a dexterity of twelve.

15
00:00:50.036 --> 00:00:55.687
Meet them all and the move becomes available, and taking it costs an ability point.

16
00:00:56.133 --> 00:01:01.822
Bonus is the move's power: it's added straight onto the roll when the move is used.

17
00:01:02.267 --> 00:01:05.783
And cooldown is how many turns before it can be used again.

18
00:01:05.783 --> 00:01:10.312
Leave it at zero unless the move would break the game if someone spammed it.

19
00:01:11.700 --> 00:01:13.876
So, what's real and what's described.

20
00:01:13.876 --> 00:01:16.053
Bonus and cooldown are exact numbers.

21
00:01:16.053 --> 00:01:18.582
Everything else, who it hits, what it does,

22
00:01:18.582 --> 00:01:22.111
how long it lasts, the narrator reads from your description.

23
00:01:22.111 --> 00:01:25.876
The more precisely you write it, the more consistently it plays.

24
00:01:27.267 --> 00:01:28.391
That's abilities.

25
00:01:28.391 --> 00:01:31.035
Our moves are linked in the description.

26
00:01:31.035 --> 00:01:35.069
Next time, skills: what your characters are actually good at.

27
00:01:35.533 --> 00:01:39.481
I'm Dreamer. Now go build something weird, and I'll see you next time!

